import{_ as t,o as a,c as s,a2 as o}from"./chunks/framework.Cdp8-jB6.js";const g=JSON.parse('{"title":"UXS-016 — the outward arc: the scale ladder, the new tiers, and a science lens on every shell","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"uxs/UXS-016.md","filePath":"uxs/UXS-016.md"}'),r={name:"uxs/UXS-016.md"};function n(i,e,l,c,h,d){return a(),s("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[o(`<h1 id="uxs-016-—-the-outward-arc-the-scale-ladder-the-new-tiers-and-a-science-lens-on-every-shell" tabindex="-1">UXS-016 — the outward arc: the scale ladder, the new tiers, and a science lens on every shell <a class="header-anchor" href="#uxs-016-—-the-outward-arc-the-scale-ladder-the-new-tiers-and-a-science-lens-on-every-shell" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;UXS-016 — the outward arc: the scale ladder, the new tiers, and a science lens on every shell&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Status · Draft v0.1 Extends · UXS-014 (navigating the known universe — the nav/breadcrumb/warp/lens contract stands; this adds the outward tiers, the scale ladder, the surface-completeness look, and the lens-everywhere UX) Related · PRD-034 (the three-pillar epic) · RFC-039 (the build contract) · #258 (scale picker, shipped) · #410 (message-objects, shipped) Visual fidelity · Signature moments get a visual anchor gating their slice (per &quot;visual anchor before UX commit&quot;). Two anchors already mocked: the <strong>8-rung scale rail</strong> and the <strong>enriched Milky Way</strong> (Milestone 1). On the operator&#39;s Desktop.</p></blockquote><h2 id="why-this-uxs-exists" tabindex="-1">Why this UXS exists <a class="header-anchor" href="#why-this-uxs-exists" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Why this UXS exists&quot;">​</a></h2><p>UXS-014 pinned <em>how it feels to move</em> through the four shells. Since then two things shipped — the <strong>#258 scale picker</strong> (a persistent scale control UXS-014 didn&#39;t have) and <strong>#410 message-objects</strong> — and PRD-034 decided to (a) <strong>extend the ladder to 8 tiers</strong>, (b) <strong>level the thin existing shells</strong>, and (c) <strong>put a science lens on every shell</strong>. This spec owns the UX of those three, so they aren&#39;t designed ad-hoc per tier. UXS-014&#39;s rules (you-always-know-where-you-are, warp-teaches-distance, honest-schematic-badging, lens-never-hides-the-exit) carry through unchanged.</p><h2 id="_1-·-the-scale-ladder-is-the-canonical-scale-control-8-rungs" tabindex="-1">1 · The scale ladder is the canonical scale control (8 rungs) <a class="header-anchor" href="#_1-·-the-scale-ladder-is-the-canonical-scale-control-8-rungs" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;1 · The scale ladder is the canonical scale control (8 rungs)&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The #258 <code>ExploreScalePicker</code> becomes the one scale control for the whole arc — grown from 4 to 8 rungs (decision: PRD-034 §UX, direction <strong>A</strong>). It reads outermost→innermost so &quot;zoom out is up&quot;:</p><div class="language- vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang"></span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span>Cosmic Web            ~14 Gpc</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>Laniakea              ~160 Mpc</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>Virgo Supercluster    ~33 Mpc</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>Local Sheet           ~10 Mpc</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>Local Group           ~3 Mpc</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>Milky Way             ~30 kpc</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>Stellar Neighbourhood ~50 pc</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>Solar System          ~100 AU     ← active rung highlighted</span></span></code></pre></div><ul><li><strong>Desktop:</strong> always-on vertical rail, lower-right, each rung = shell name + scale label; active rung highlighted (cyan), sub-view takeovers hide it (as #258 already does).</li><li><strong>Mobile:</strong> the same collapse-to-&quot;Scale ▾&quot; chip → popover; the popover now lists 8 rungs (auto-closes on pick). If 8 rungs prove too tall on a small viewport, the RFC-039 fallback (the C-hybrid spectrum) is a contained swap — same control, different presentation.</li><li><strong>Every rung is a warp</strong> (UXS-014): picking a distant rung drives the existing multi-step <code>contextDeepLinkFn</code> walk, each crossing captioned with the distance it teaches (&quot;65 million light-years to the Virgo Cluster…&quot;). The breadcrumb extends in lockstep: <code>Solar System › … › Local Group › Local Sheet › Virgo</code>.</li></ul><h2 id="_2-·-the-four-new-outward-tiers-—-how-they-read" tabindex="-1">2 · The four new outward tiers — how they read <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-·-the-four-new-outward-tiers-—-how-they-read" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;2 · The four new outward tiers — how they read&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Each new tier follows the Local Group shell&#39;s visual grammar (schematic sprites + labels + a &quot;you are here&quot; anchor for the shell one level in), and <strong>must</strong> carry the honest-schematic badge (UXS-014 · PRD-030 principle 2) — now with a learn-more link (fixing the LG badge&#39;s missing one):</p><ul><li><strong>Local Sheet</strong> — the Local Group as a blob among the M81 group, Centaurus A, Sculptor; anchor = &quot;Local Group ⌾&quot;.</li><li><strong>Virgo Supercluster</strong> — the Virgo Cluster (M87 as the highlighted BCG) + Fornax; our supercluster plane; anchor = &quot;Local Sheet ⌾&quot;.</li><li><strong>Laniakea</strong> — the flow-basin toward the Great Attractor (Norma), Coma, Perseus-Pisces; velocity-flow streamlines under the Hubble-flow lens; anchor = &quot;Virgo Cluster ⌾&quot;.</li><li><strong>Cosmic Web</strong> — filaments, walls, voids → the observable-universe / CMB boundary. The most schematic tier: heaviest &quot;this is a model&quot; badging, no implied precision.</li></ul><p>Selecting a cluster/galaxy opens a panel (the LocalGroupPanel family, extended with member count / BCG / recession velocity / a learn-more link). Two doors in, per UXS-014: wander, or jump via <code>?context=&lt;tier&gt;</code> / a gallery/index <code>?goto=</code>.</p><h2 id="_3-·-milestone-1-—-the-enriched-milky-way-the-first-build-mock-gated" tabindex="-1">3 · Milestone 1 — the enriched Milky Way (the first build, mock-gated) <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-·-milestone-1-—-the-enriched-milky-way-the-first-build-mock-gated" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;3 · Milestone 1 — the enriched Milky Way (the first build, mock-gated)&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The Milky Way shell today is 2 clickable objects and no lens (RFC-039 §4). The enriched look (mocked, on the operator&#39;s Desktop) adds, on the existing gorgeous spiral:</p><ul><li><strong>The galactic bar</strong> — a subtle elongated core glow, labelled (the science article already claims a barred spiral).</li><li><strong>A globular-cluster halo</strong> — the ~30 globulars already in the data, pinned above/below the disc; headliners labelled (ω Centauri, 47 Tuc, M13). Clickable → panel + article.</li><li><strong>The Magellanic Clouds</strong> — LMC + SMC as fuzzy companions at the disc edge (they&#39;re gravitationally MW, conceptually in-shell).</li><li><strong>Arm interactivity</strong> — each arm label becomes a clickable chip → arm panel/article (today they&#39;re dead sprites).</li><li><strong>The scale HUD</strong> — un-suppressed: a kpc scale bar + &quot;Milky Way · ~30 kpc across&quot; (today the MW shell shows no distance reference at all).</li><li><strong>The first MW science lens</strong> — chips for <strong>Rotation curve</strong>, <strong>Dark-matter halo</strong>, <strong>Stellar populations</strong> (§4). This proves the per-shell lens pattern the rest of the epic reuses.</li></ul><p>Interaction stays within UXS-014&#39;s model (click-a-pin, breadcrumb, lens-toggle). This look is <strong>mock-gated before the slice</strong> (anchor delivered).</p><h2 id="_4-·-a-science-lens-on-every-shell-the-chip-taxonomy-the-ux" tabindex="-1">4 · A science lens on every shell + the chip taxonomy (the UX) <a class="header-anchor" href="#_4-·-a-science-lens-on-every-shell-the-chip-taxonomy-the-ux" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;4 · A science lens on every shell + the chip taxonomy (the UX)&quot;">​</a></h2><p>PRD-034 pillar 3 / RFC-039 Contract D, as felt by the user:</p><ul><li><strong>The lens is the single home for &quot;this teaches you something.&quot;</strong> Every shell — including the Milky Way and Local Group, which have none today — gets a science-lens surface (the <code>ScienceLayersPanel</code> or the neighborhood&#39;s inline lens-chip pattern, unified).</li><li><strong>Two visually distinct chip families:</strong><ul><li><strong>Service chips</strong> (always-on, no lens gate) — pure visibility toggles: PLANETS, DWARFS, COMETS, INTERSTELLAR, PATHS. Neutral/slate styling.</li><li><strong>Teaching chips</strong> (inside the science lens) — DEEP-SKY, CONSTELLATIONS, HR-diagram, light-cones, and the new cosmology lenses (distance-ladder, Hubble-flow, dark-matter-web, redshift). Cyan &quot;lens&quot; styling; each carries a <code>→ science</code> learn link into its article.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Turning the lens on</strong> reveals the teaching chips for the active shell and nothing meaningless (only context-relevant lenses show — UXS-014). Turning it off leaves the service chips + the honest scene. The breadcrumb + exit are never hidden.</li><li><strong>New cosmology lenses read as overlays on the same scene</strong>, never separate screens (UXS-014): distance-ladder draws the parallax→Cepheid→SN Ia rungs; Hubble-flow draws recession vectors; dark-matter-web tints the filament mass; redshift colours galaxies by z.</li></ul><h2 id="_5-·-the-learning-surface-surfaced-the-cosmology-articles" tabindex="-1">5 · The learning surface, surfaced (the cosmology articles) <a class="header-anchor" href="#_5-·-the-learning-surface-surfaced-the-cosmology-articles" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;5 · The learning surface, surfaced (the cosmology articles)&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Every new tier and lens links <strong>out</strong> to a backing /science article (the <code>see_in_app</code> ↔ learn-link loop, UXS-014). The new cosmology set (Big Bang, nucleosynthesis, carbon/CNO, distance ladder, redshift/Hubble, dark matter/energy, CMB, large-scale structure — RFC-039 §6) is reachable from the lens chips and the tier badges, so the atlas always answers &quot;how do we know?&quot; No tier ships without its story.</p><h2 id="_6-·-responsive-a11y-honesty-carried-from-uxs-014" tabindex="-1">6 · Responsive, a11y, honesty (carried from UXS-014) <a class="header-anchor" href="#_6-·-responsive-a11y-honesty-carried-from-uxs-014" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;6 · Responsive, a11y, honesty (carried from UXS-014)&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Mobile parity</strong> on core nav (ladder popover, warp, select, breadcrumb, lens); density adapts to the device budget; heaviest cosmology shaders desktop-first with a legible mobile tier.</li><li><strong>A11y:</strong> the object/tier index is keyboard-reachable via the DOM mirror + <code>?context=</code>/<code>?goto=</code>; warps announce destinations; reduced-motion shortens the crossings.</li><li><strong>Honesty:</strong> every super-galactic tier is schematic and badged; the Cosmic Web tier&#39;s badge is the loudest. Culture-door / fiction badging unchanged.</li></ul><h2 id="_7-·-signature-moments-that-get-a-visual-anchor-before-their-slice" tabindex="-1">7 · Signature moments that get a visual anchor before their slice <a class="header-anchor" href="#_7-·-signature-moments-that-get-a-visual-anchor-before-their-slice" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;7 · Signature moments that get a visual anchor before their slice&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>The enriched Milky Way</strong> (Milestone 1) — ✅ mocked.</li><li><strong>The 8-rung scale rail</strong> (desktop + mobile popover) — ✅ mocked (direction A).</li><li><strong>Each outward boundary crossing</strong> — the collapse-and-rebase (Local Group → Local Sheet, etc.) + distance caption, per tier.</li><li><strong>A new cosmology lens toggle</strong> — the scene re-rendered through physics (Hubble-flow vectors / dark-matter web).</li></ol><p>3 and 4 are mocked/prototyped on real frames and gated on the operator&#39;s approval before their slices ship.</p><hr><p><em>UXS-016 · draft · 2026-08-08 — the outward arc&#39;s interaction spec: the 8-rung ladder, the new tiers, the Milky-Way-first enrichment, and the science-lens-everywhere + chip taxonomy. Extends UXS-014.</em></p>`,28)])])}const p=t(r,[["render",n]]);export{g as __pageData,p as default};
